quran[23]{c,v,t}:
  89,1,"By the dawn,*"
  89,2,"and by the ten nights,*"
  89,3,"and by the even and the odd,*"
  89,4,and by the night when it departs!*
  89,5,"Surely, there is an oath in it for the one possessing wisdom."
  89,6,"Have you not seen how your Lord dealt with (the people of) ‘Ad,"
  89,7,"and (the people of) Iram, (the city) of the towering castles,"
  89,8,"the likes of which had not been created in the countries (at that time),"
  89,9,"and (the people of) Thamud, who carved out (their homes in) the rocks in the (Qura) valley,"
  89,10,"and Pharaoh, the possessor of large armies?"
  89,11,"(They were) those who rebelled (against Allah) in the lands,"
  89,12,and spread much corruption therein.
  89,13,So your Lord unleashed the scourge of punishment upon them.
  89,14,"Indeed, your Lord is (always) on watch."
  89,15,"As for the human being, whenever his Lord tests him, grants him honour and blesses him (with bounties), he says: ‘My Lord has honoured me.’"
  89,16,"But when He tests him and tightens his provision, he says: ‘My Lord has humiliated me.’"
  89,17,"No, indeed! Instead, you do not honour the orphan,"
  89,18,"and you do not urge one another to feed the poor,"
  89,19,"and you eat away the inheritance (neglecting others) greedily,"
  89,20,and you love wealth with an exceeding passion.
  89,21,"No, indeed! When the earth is crumbled into pieces and pounded to dust particles,"
  89,22,"and your Lord comes (to judge), with the angels (appearing) in rows upon rows,"
  89,23,"(and) Hell is brought (closer) that Day. On that Day, humans will become mindful of advice, but what will be the benefit of remembering then?"
